# D10(b) over-rejection guard — the writer-Copy-read exemption: a `&` writer of
# the whole place and a bare read of an overlapping COPY sub-place
# (`f(&s, s.tag)` where `s.tag` is an `int`). The Copy read is evaluated at the
# call site into an INDEPENDENT value before the callee runs — no live memory
# edge remains between it and the writer's region, so there is nothing to
# diverge against. The rule ranges over LIVE ALIASES, not syntactic reads:
# a Copy-typed bare read participates in no overlap (D10(b) ADDENDUM +
# Rider 1 REVISED). Must ACCEPT and lower. Copy-ness is read from the TYPED
# axis (`int` → scalar primitive → Copy), never the value shape.
struct S:
    Vector[int] data
    int tag

void f(S &a, int t):
    a.data.push(t)

void run():
    S s = S(Vector[int](), 7)
    f(&s, s.tag)

void main():
    run()
